{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Va'echazt.</b> Some interpret: the name of a person." "<b>His companion (mere'ehu).</b> His friend, and the mem in it is a root letter, as in ויתנה למרעהו. And so we find in the Masorah, on ואחזת: there is no other instance like it."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The phrase לית שום בר אינש (lit. 'there is no son of man') is obscure in context; rendered here as a Masoretic note indicating uniqueness of this form. The meaning is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:08.074202122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}